    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="instruction-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">STNT1W (vector plus scalar)</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Scatter store non-temporal words</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">This instruction performs a non-temporal scatter store of  words from the Active
elements of a vector register to the memory addresses generated by a
vector base plus a 64-bit unscaled scalar register offset.
Inactive elements are not written to memory.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">A non-temporal store is a hint to the system that this data is
unlikely to be referenced again soon.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">This instruction is illegal when executed in Streaming SVE mode, unless FEAT_SME_FA64 is implemented and enabled.</p>
    
    <p class="desc">
      It has encodings from 2 classes:
      <a href="#iclass_32_bit_unscaled_offset">32-bit unscaled offset</a>
       and 
      <a href="#iclass_64_bit_unscaled_offset">64-bit unscaled offset</a>
    </p>
    <h3 class="classheading"><a id="iclass_32_bit_unscaled_offset"></a>32-bit unscaled offset class
